From 1f14a155334382fbd722fdb46f39f7adac1b2d66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shi3z <shi3z@me.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 05:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] llama: static hot-expert split for host-resident MoE
 layers (LLAMA_MOE_HOT_LIST)

The listed experts of each layer are gathered into GPU tensors at load; the graph runs the
selected hot experts on the GPU and the host chain on the rest (hot slots point at a masked dummy
so the ids stay valid for the large-batch expert copy). Sized from llama-moe-routing-stats.
Also: CPU mul_mat_id skips negative ids (unused by the default path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
